# MiniTool HQ — SEO / long-tail keywords (mandatory)

If customers cannot find the tool in search, the tool has no business value.  
**Do not mark a tool shipped** until the SEO checklist below is complete on the live tool page + spec.

## SEO expert skill (hard)

Before any SEO work (new tool/guide SEO, audit, sitemap, GSC, on-page/meta/FAQ/JSON-LD, internal links), **Read and follow** `.cursor/skills/minitool-seo-expert/SKILL.md`.  
Rule: `.cursor/rules/minitool-seo-expert.mdc`. Do not skip the skill.

## Customer-first product rule (hard)

**Same customer job = one tool.** Do **not** ship separate tools that only change a marketplace preset (e.g. Amazon image prep vs TikTok image prep vs Etsy image prep).

- Cover vertical search phrases (**amazon product image resize**, **tiktok shop image size**, etc.) on **that one page** via Title/H1/lede, platform picker labels, requirements table rows, and FAQ questions.
- Optional: old vanity URLs may **redirect** into the one tool with `?platform=…` — never maintain duplicate UIs.
- Split tools only when the **job is different** (e.g. FBA box Pass/Fail ≠ image resize).

## Spec (before coding)

In `docs/specs/NN-*.md` under **Meta** + **SEO**:

| Field | Required |
|-------|----------|
| Primary keyword | 1 phrase users actually type |
| Secondary keywords | **≥3** related long-tails (may include other platforms’ phrases if one tool covers them) |
| Title | Includes primary; under ~60 chars when possible |
| H1 | Includes primary (or closest natural variant) |
| Meta description | Includes primary + ≥1 secondary; job outcome; under ~160 chars |
| FAQ topics | ≥5 questions that mirror search queries (not only product FAQ) |

## Tool page (must ship together with the feature)

1. **`<title>` + meta description + canonical + OG/Twitter** via `BaseLayout`
2. **H1** carries the primary keyword
3. **Opening lede** naturally uses primary + secondary phrases (no keyword stuffing)
4. **FAQ** ≥5 items; questions worded like real searches
5. **FAQPage JSON-LD** must include **every** on-page FAQ (same source array — do not maintain two copies)
6. **WebApplication JSON-LD** with name, description, url, `offers.price: "0"` when free
7. **Rules / requirements table** when the job is policy-driven
8. **Homepage** Tools card links to the tool with a keyword-relevant title
9. **Sitemap** picks up the URL via `@astrojs/sitemap` (no orphan pages)

## E2E gate (before “shipped”)

Tool E2E **must** assert at least:

- `document.title` contains the primary keyword (or agreed Title fragment from the spec)
- `meta[name="description"]` is non-empty and contains the primary keyword
- On-page FAQ count ≥ 5
- FAQPage JSON-LD script exists and question count ≥ on-page FAQ count
- H1 is present and matches the keyword intent from the spec

## Do / Don’t

- Do: one strong tool URL; rank nearby long-tails via FAQ/table/platform copy
- Do: sync SEO when renaming the tool or changing the job
- Don’t: split one job into many tools “for SEO”
- Don’t: ship UI-only and “add SEO later”
- Don’t: use a bare `meta keywords` tag as the strategy
- Don’t: put internal strategy jargon in titles/FAQs (see `minitool-customer-copy.mdc`)

## Monetization note

**All MiniTool HQ tools are fully free.** Revenue is display ads. Do not ship Pro paywalls or $4.99 membership CTAs.
